<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">DEPLOYMENT MODELS</span><h1>Fit the edge<br><em>to your network.</em></h1><p class="lede">Choose a boundary: focused translation, a combined subscriber edge or a repeatable regional design. These are evaluation architectures, not validated production guarantees.</p></section><section class="section"><span class="eyebrow">THREE STARTING POINTS</span><h2>Keep the scope deliberate.</h2><div class="cards"><article><h3>Standalone CGNAT</h3><p>Keep your BNG and AAA systems while evaluating translation behind them. Define subscriber correlation, traffic symmetry, public pool ownership, logging and route withdrawal.</p></article><article><h3>Combined broadband edge</h3><p>Evaluate subscriber access, policy, addressing and translation together. Include your handoff, RADIUS attributes, CPE behaviour, IPv6 delegation and service changes.</p></article><article><h3>Regional gateways</h3><p>Repeat a gateway pattern near subscribers. Separate local redundancy from site recovery, and define what must survive loss of central management.</p></article></div></section><section class="section"><span class="eyebrow">WRITE THE DESIGN</span><h2>What belongs in the deployment plan?</h2><div class="cards"><article><h3>Physical & virtual platform</h3><p>CPU topology, NIC queues, firmware, PCIe placement, memory, NUMA and virtualisation boundaries. Interface speed does not establish forwarding capacity.</p></article><article><h3>Management boundary</h3><p>Reachable management access, time, certificates and a recovery console. Keep web services outside the packet path.</p></article><article><h3>Routing & ownership</h3><p>Who announces subscriber and public pools? How are routes withdrawn? Which node may own an address after a partition?</p></article><article><h3>Operational dependencies</h3><p>Document AAA, billing, DNS, logging, storage and monitoring. Decide whether each outage blocks admission, affects existing service or reduces visibility.</p></article></div></section><section class="editorial"><span class="eyebrow">THE NEXT STEP</span><h2>Bring a drawing.<br>Leave with a test boundary.</h2><p>A useful topology review ends with traffic paths, ownership, failure domains, dependencies and measurable acceptance criteria.</p><a class="button" href="contact.php">Discuss your deployment ↗</a> <a class="text-link" href="performance.php">Build the workload profile →</a></section>
